   {
    "question": "Using the formulae for $\\sin(A+B)$ and $\\cos(A+B)$, prove that\n$\\tan(A + B) = \\dfrac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}$.",
    "level": "higher",
    "marks": 10,
    "workedSolution": {
     "steps": [
      {
       "title": "Write tan as sine over cosine",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "$\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ for any angle $\\theta$."
        },
        {
         "tex": "\\tan(A+B) &= \\frac{\\sin(A+B)}{\\cos(A+B)}",
         "sym": "Eq(tan(A+B), sin(A+B)/cos(A+B))"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Expand the sine and cosine",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "Use the formulae for $\\sin(A+B)$ and $\\cos(A+B)$ with the angles $A$ and $B$."
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= \\frac{\\sin A \\cos B + \\cos A \\sin B}{\\cos A \\cos B - \\sin A \\sin B}",
         "sym": "Eq(tan(A+B), (sin(A)*cos(B)+cos(A)*sin(B))/(cos(A)*cos(B)-sin(A)*sin(B)))"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Divide top and bottom by the same term",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "Divide every term by $\\cos A \\cos B$ (not zero, since the tangents exist)."
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= \\frac{\\dfrac{\\sin A \\cos B}{\\cos A \\cos B} + \\dfrac{\\cos A \\sin B}{\\cos A \\cos B}}{\\dfrac{\\cos A \\cos B}{\\cos A \\cos B} - \\dfrac{\\sin A \\sin B}{\\cos A \\cos B}}",
         "sym": "Eq(tan(A+B), (sin(A)*cos(B)/(cos(A)*cos(B))+cos(A)*sin(B)/(cos(A)*cos(B)))/(cos(A)*cos(B)/(cos(A)*cos(B))-sin(A)*sin(B)/(cos(A)*cos(B))))"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Cancel to get tangents",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "$\\dfrac{\\sin A}{\\cos A} = \\tan A$ and $\\dfrac{\\sin B}{\\cos B} = \\tan B$."
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}",
         "sym": "Eq(tan(A+B), (tan(A)+tan(B))/(1-tan(A)*tan(B)))"
        },
        {
         "text": "So $\\tan(A+B) = \\dfrac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}$, as required."
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "finalAnswer": "\\tan(A+B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}"
    },
    "finalSym": "0",
    "answerSym": "simplify(expand_trig(tan(A+B)) - (tan(A)+tan(B))/(1-tan(A)*tan(B)))"
   },
